WEBVTT

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:27.130
Sukemori, reflect upon your
discourtesy toward Lord Motofusa

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.340
and conduct yourself accordingly in Ise.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.300
Yes, Father.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.350
Mother...

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.740
Must we really send Sukemori to Ise?

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.990
He already received punishment
for the impoliteness

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.990
he showed His Highness the regent.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:58.160
It was not him that ordered
300 riders to attack 10 men!

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.050
They say it was so much
that it made Motofusa cry.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:17.310
I have dismissed everyone
who attacked Lord Motofusa

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.140
and sent Sukemori to Ise.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.770
You really are a bore, you know.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.150
As a result of this incident,

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.070
the ranks of those who are not
amused by the Heike have grown.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.320
All right. I get it.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.780
I know.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.240
On account of the trouble I
caused you, I'll get you a gift.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.960
How about one of those
lanterns you're so fond of?

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.540
The word is that you put up
48 lanterns in your estate.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.550
Some call you Lantern Lord.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.630
Are you that frightened of the dark?

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.930
Hey, baldy!

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.260
What would a gaudy man like you
know of the dark's terror?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.850
Biwa!

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.520
Remember this:

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.730
Darkness always lies just ahead!

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.820
Now you are amusing.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:33.170
THE HEIKE STORY

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.670
H-Hey!

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.420
Episode 2

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:50.960
Tokiko!

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.340
What are you doing?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.210
Ow, ow, ow.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.630
A warrior imitating the nobles!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.760
Do you intend to set your hands
on Lord Shigemori's child?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.930
Let me go!

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:01.970
Let me go, Shige--

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.850
Oh. Sorry.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.100
Brother?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.310
Tokuko?

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.110
Father said he wanted
to keep you at his side?

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.940
But my brother turned him down, right?

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.950
Thank goodness.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.620
This is my fault.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.780
It was my request,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.580
that he bring you with him.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.580
Since my little sister Moriko
married 6 years ago,

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.840
I've had no one I can open up to.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.670
Moriko became Lord Fujiwara no
Motozane's bride at the age of nine.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:43.470
Even though Lord Motozane already had
a five-year-old son with another woman.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.510
A political marriage.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:52.100
But in the end, Lord Motozane
passed two years after marrying Moriko.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.520
Moriko was a widow at age 11.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.070
What's more, she became
a parent to his son.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:07.080
Oh, Lord Motozane was the
older brother of Lord Motofusa.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:13.290
So Moriko essentially acquired lands
and assets of the Fujiwara clan.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:20.010
Motofusa's displeasure at that might be
the reason Sukemori was treated so badly.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.930
In the end, Father thinks
of us only as his pawns.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.940
Though it's not just us...

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:53.710
It looks like I have to
get married now too.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:57.170
I'm 16, marrying a boy a
whole six years my junior.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:59.000
That's really young.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.420
And get this. His father is...

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.470
My throat hurts.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.640
Father, it stinks.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:14.520
Your father is drinking garlic chive
water because he feels unwell.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:19.020
Is that not because he was singing
imayo songs all through the night?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.860
I could hear him even from my room.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:26.320
♬ When I spy a lovely maiden, ♬

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.370
♬ I wish us to be vines
twisted together as one. ♬

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:36.750
Imayo songs are like a mirror that
reflects the world in the present!

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.710
Wanting to be a vine twisted
with a beautiful woman.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:44.670
What value is there in a mirror
that reflects such a thing?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.300
Norihito!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.010
Excuse me, Father.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.230
Shigeko!

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:02.280
That boy has gotten so mouthy since his
coming-of-age ceremony was scheduled!

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:07.070
But is it not rather reassuring
that he can speak his mind?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.410
It means he will be no one's puppet.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:13.040
Not even when he is wed to
Lord Kiyomori's daughter.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:15.500
Hmph. Kiyomori's daughter...

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:20.710
Norihito requires powerful backing.
He needs the strength of the Heike.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.510
But what if Kiyomori
ends up pulling the strings?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.340
Then that will be a situation
for <i>you </i>to handle, my lord.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.390
To put it in imayo terms,
Lord Kiyomori is the snail.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.100
The snail?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.100
If he does not do as you say...

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.850
Ah, then I kick him!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:45.240
♬ Dance, little snail, dance!
For if you don't... ♬

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:50.820
♬ ...I shall have the foals
and calves kick you. ♬

00:07:55.500 --> 00:08:00.380
Thanks for listening to me
for so long, Biwa.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.840
Come visit again.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.300
What's wrong?

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.720
It's nothing.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.680
Ma?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.480
Ma!

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.640
Oh...

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.270
...you're not her.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.520
What is your name?

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.400
Biwa.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.900
Is your mother a shirabyoshi too?

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.030
That's what Pa said.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.240
I see.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.580
That's Lady Gio and her
younger sister Lady Ginyo.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.170
They're here for Hotoke-Gozen
to chat with.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.380
Oh...

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:53.510
Well, you see, at one time,
Gio was Father's favorite.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.970
But after he began to favor a
shirabyoshi named Hotoke-Gozen,

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.140
he kicked Lady Gio out.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.980
Yet she started to be summoned here again,

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:06.480
because Hotoke-Gozen seems
lonely with no one to talk to.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:11.780
There's no telling what Father
would do to her if she refused.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.540
"Lantern Lord," huh?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.340
The dark has frightened
me since I was a child.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:34.050
Perhaps because of what I see.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.060
What frightens you, Biwa?

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:48.020
The future.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.280
The future frightens me.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.620
I see.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.670
Though the future and the
dark may be frightening,

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.330
this present moment...

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.000
...is beautiful.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:16.470
You resign as Major Counselor?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.390
Because of the attack on the regent?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:23.020
Aren't you supposed to handle
Norihito's coming-of-age ceremony?

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:23.980
Yes.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:29.230
I ask your leave to have my brother
Munemori take over in my stead.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.570
You're cleaning the shit up thoroughly.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:34.490
You fired the men who assaulted Motofusa,

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:38.330
and confined your son,
the cause of the commotion, in Ise,

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.870
and now you take responsibility too.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.870
It is only proper, my lord.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:48.460
I acknowledge the trouble
I have caused you.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.460
What is Kiyomori doing?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:53.760
Devoting himself to building
lodging in Fukuhara?

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.680
Yes. But he occasionally
visits the capital.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.800
I hear he has taken a
liking to a shirabyoshi.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:05.060
Despite entering monastic life, he seems
very attached to worldly affairs.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:09.730
I did it in order to abdicate
the throne to Norihito.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.570
But it seems Kiyomori shaved his head

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.200
to avoid responsibilities
and do as he pleases.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:22.950
Ultimately I serve not my father but you,
my lord, as well as Lord Norihito.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.970
Your turn, my lord.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:45.560
That Shigemori is one upstanding fellow.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:51.110
There is a reason he is referred to
as the conscience of the Heike.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.610
He is a renowned warrior.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.820
In the Heiji rebellion...

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:58.530
The era is Heiji, the capital is Heian,
and we bear the Hei name!

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.410
All use the "hei" character!

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.950
So let us pacify the enemy!

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:08.040
...it's said that's how
he roused his comrades.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:13.250
Yes, but while he is the
eldest son, Shigemori is...

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.380
...is not Tokiko's child?

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:21.430
Last year, when Fujiwara no Narichika
had a dispute with Enryakuji Temple

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:25.680
and Enryakuji marched to
demand Narichika's exile,

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.060
I ordered Shigemori to fight. But...

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:32.270
As I am under orders,
I have come prepared for battle.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.820
However, I humbly ask that this course
against the monks be reconsidered.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:42.620
It was such a good opportunity to chip
away at that bothersome temple's power.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:49.250
Despite my orders, the Heike must not have
wanted to make an enemy of Enryakuji.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.460
And the one behind that was...

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:59.050
Still, my lord, Shigemori will eventually
be leader not just in name.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:02.340
Shigemori places his
loyalty firmly with you.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.430
And if you welcome
his little sister Tokuko,

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.980
the might of the Heike will
wind up protecting Norihito.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:11.480
That's right.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:13.650
Cast the dice.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:18.110
Three things defy my plans:
the sugoroku dice,

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.950
the waters of the Kamo river,

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.570
and Enryakuji's monks.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.240
Well expressed indeed.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:27.200
Now, what will happen with the Heike?

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:32.120
Biwa, are you going to Rokuhara again?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:36.590
Sukemori is in Ise.
I'll have no one to play with.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.880
I'll play after I return.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.050
Pretentious.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.220
It's just birds.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.060
I know.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.930
I was just startled.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.280
Biwa!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.070
Tokuko!

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.410
She's here.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.130
Gio.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.420
That was pretty!

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.800
It was so, so pretty!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.430
Your notes were lovely as well, Biwa.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.600
There's plenty more.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.730
Listen, Biwa.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.440
My mother is also a shirabyoshi.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:29.660
She has heard of a shirabyoshi whose
eyes are different colors, like yours.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.660
One that supposedly had a child.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:35.620
But a nobleman took quite a liking to her,

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.670
and she was supposedly
forced to go with him.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.920
Is it my ma?

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.840
I cannot say for sure.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.010
Where is this person now?

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:48.390
My mother never met her, so...

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:52.850
Biwa, I'll also ask around about her.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:56.850
I'm sure you'll meet her, one day.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:01.360
"One day" is a nice phrase.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.400
Tomorrow.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.030
The next day.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:08.820
Now I can look forward
to the future a little.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:14.200
Well, I need to go keep
Lady Hotoke-Gozen company now.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.210
Gio, show me your dance again next time.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.130
"Next time."

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.960
That too is a nice phrase.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.290
Biwa, what's with the vacant stare?

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.700
Koremori...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.250
Biwa!

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.330
Tokuko!

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.420
It's been a while.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.380
Hello, Koremori.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:06.670
Tokuko, when is "next time?"

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.050
When is my "next time" with Gio?

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.760
I'm afraid that...

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:29.240
Are you all right?

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.700
My little sister, my mother,
and I became nuns.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:43.540
I was resentful.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:48.960
He saw me only when he pleased, and when
his interest shifted, I had to obey.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:52.720
It was just as if I were
Lord Kiyomori's pawn.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.720
But from now on I can live in peace.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.520
Yeah.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:03.940
You must be upset there
can be no next time.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.980
♬ Worldly wealth is but an illusion. ♬

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:47.110
♬ What good can riches do us? ♬

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:51.530
♬ I stand before you with a shaved head. ♬

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:56.030
♬ Forgive me, I beg, for my past sins. ♬

00:18:56.030 --> 00:19:02.250
♬ If you deign to forgive me, ♬

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:08.840
♬ let us all live together in prayer, ♬

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:15.130
♬ and be born on the same lotus in Paradise. ♬

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.320
Tomorrow.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.860
The next day.

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:34.240
After this. In the future.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:37.910
Far in the future. Even farther.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:39.950
Good things happen too.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:41.580
Yes.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:45.160
Both Hotoke-Gozen and
Gio's faces were serene.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.170
I want to tell Tokuko too!

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.050
Tokuko has been betrothed.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:56.630
At the end of the year, she'll be
wed into the imperial family.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:14.990
Tokuko!

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.240
Biwa.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.740
I'm sorry I've been unable to see you.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.660
I've been busy with preparations.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:25.870
Don't go!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.790
Don't go!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.590
Stop!

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:39.010
Thank you, Biwa.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:41.760
I'm grateful for your concern.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.060
But, I'll be all right.

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:48.440
And this doesn't mean we
can never see each other.

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:51.060
Until next time. Right?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.060
Tokuko!
